From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:20:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sessions): outcome refresh off the messaging reply path;
 a judge's verdict survives judge-less refreshes; judges get the source
 [daveey]

- gateway turn end no longer awaits the outcome refresh before the reply reaches the adapter: it runs on a
  daemon thread that keeps the turn's context (profile scope).
- A judged outcome stores judged=true and the judged message id; a refresh in a process without a judge
  (CLI outcome-audit --refresh, web ?refresh=1) keeps that verdict for the same message instead of letting
  the heuristic overwrite it.
- Judges are called as fn(sid, text, source=...) with the row's sessions.source; a judge without the
  keyword is called as fn(sid, text).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
